      "content": [
        {
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "The pattern indexes most consistently as an **orthorhombic primitive cell**, approximately\n\n\\[\na=5.511\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad b=7.076\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad c=8.827\\ \\text{\u00c5},\n\\]\n\nwith \\(Z=4\\). The systematic absences and composition support **Pnma (No. 62)** and an \\(oP32\\) GaNi\\(_6\\)B-type model. Representative low-angle indexing is \\(011,101,110,111,020,120,121,200,210,\\ldots\\). The calculated density is about \\(8.35\\ \\mathrm{g\\,cm^{-3}}\\).\n\nThe cell and space-group assignment are substantially more secure than the light-element coordinate: Cu X-ray data constrain B relatively weakly. The coordinates below are therefore a prototype-constrained primary model suitable for final Rietveld refinement.\n\n```cif\ndata_GaNi6B_primary\n_audit_creation_method              'Powder indexing and prototype-constrained structure solution'\n_chemical_name_common               'gallium hexanickel boride'\n_chemical_formula_sum                'B Ga Ni6'\n_chemical_formula_structural         'GaNi6B'\n_cell_formula_units_Z                4\n\n_cell_length_a                       5.511\n_cell_length_b                       7.076\n_cell_length_c                       8.827\n_cell_angle_alpha                    90\n_cell_angle_beta                     90\n_cell_angle_gamma                    90\n_cell_volume                         344.25\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn        8.35\n_diffrn_radiation_type               'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength         1.5406\n\n_space_group_crystal_system          orthorhombic\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt            'P n m a'\n_space_group_IT_number               62\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  'x+1/2,-y+1/2,-z+1/2'\n3  '-x,y+1/2,-z'\n4  '-x+1/2,-y,z+1/2'\n5  '-x,-y,-z'\n6  '-x+1/2,y+1/2,z+1/2'\n7  'x,-y+1/2,z'\n8  'x+1/2,y,-z+1/2'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nGa1  Ga  4  c  0.0195  0.2500  0.6850  1.0  0.60\nB1   B   4  c  0.1810  0.2500  0.0640  1.0  0.80\nNi1  Ni  8  d  0.1605  0.0555  0.3195  1.0  0.50\nNi2  Ni  8  d  0.2190  0.0580  0.8195  1.0  0.50\nNi3  Ni  8  d  0.4050  0.0560  0.1790  1.0  0.50\n```\n\nNo distinct alternative Bravais lattice survives the low-angle indexing comparably well. Axis permutations or origin-equivalent settings of Pnma are, of course, crystallographically equivalent. The principal remaining uncertainty is refinement of the fractional coordinates\u2014especially B\u2014rather than the unit cell or space group.",
